From: Randy Eckenrode <randy@largeandhighquality.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Jan 2026 14:37:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Read C and C++ stdlib flags from the wrapped compiler
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On most platforms supported by Nixpkgs, the C and C++ standard libraries
are located separately and are not part of the sysroot, but Swift’s
ClangImporter assumes they are part of the sysroot by default.

While it is possible to create a sysroot for use with Swift, this has
negative affects on every package that wants to use Swift and compile
C++ code. The C++ library must be removed from the standard platform
configuration, which makes adding Swift as a dependency too disruptive.
